From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Anothers <14343424+Anothers@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 12:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 92/92] dsv41: retain 4K prefill workspace above floor and cap
 sub-4K replay tails to AOT

When TF_DSV41_PF_4K=1 is enabled under replay prefill, two overheads penalised
multi-turn traffic on unified-memory GB10 nodes:
1. Prompts and incremental turns shorter than 4,096 tokens still ran wsAgreed
   and dispatched unaligned 2,049..4,095-row single segments, missing prebuilt
   2,048- and 4,096-row AOT Triton captures and stalling 1.5-3.6 s in runtime
   JIT compilation.
2. k4Release unconditionally freed the ~2.3 GiB K4 workspace after every
   prefill, paying cuMemAlloc + memset + cuMemFree page-reclaim stalls on
   every subsequent >= 4,096-token prompt even with ample free memory.

Skip wsAgreed when neither K4 (ids.len >= 4096) nor TBO pair prefill needs it,
cap sub-4096 single segments in replay mode at prefill_rows (singleRows) so
every tail hits AOT shapes, and retain k4ws.buf in k4Release whenever all TP
ranks agree via Agreement that MemAvailable >= wsFloorGiB() (freeing it
synchronously across all ranks as soon as any rank dips below the floor).

Includes host unit tests in review_workspace_test.zig that fail on unpatched
main. Verified 20/20 greedy replay SHA-256 bit-exact (15,813 tokens) on 2x
GB10 TP=2.
